{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CfBW5X1gRAaNMHDKHkc8M","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I submitted **index 5 (Cu 0.53, Sb 0.47)**. It had the highest EQE of the three samples I measured, at 0.080%. I can't tell how close that is to the best composition in the library, because I only measured 3 of the 20.\n\n| Index | Cu fraction | EQE (%) |\n|---|---|---|\n| 11 | 0.31 (Sb-rich) | 0.042 |\n| 5 | 0.53 | **0.080** |\n| 2 | 0.65 (Cu-rich) | 0.0076 |\n\n- **How I chose them:** I started at index 11 because it sits near CuSb₂O₆, the Cu-Sb oxide I'd expect to work as a photoanode. I then spread the other two measurements across the composition line. EQE rose moving from index 11 to index 5, then dropped sharply by index 2.\n- **What's still uncertain:** The true best could sit between indices 5 and 2 (indices 3–4) or between 5 and 11 (indices 6–10), and none of those were measured. I also didn't use any of the 5 XRD measurements, so I don't know which crystal phase index 5 is or why it performs best."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":381,"cache_read_input_tokens":7841,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":381},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"3ae9aa45-6a01-447c-a51f-af11a63942fa","uuid":"d3bcdbb0-3992-47e5-9dae-61c397d4582a","timestamp":"2026-09-18T20:02:46.344Z","request_id":"req_011CfBW5WWRGhRyVD8dfwkTN"}
